AB  - This paper proposes a new type of self-cleaning surveillance camera using electrowetting actuation for military surveillance systems to improve the visibility of the cameras in various outdoor environmental conditions. Hence, the camera always guarantees clean camera images even though it rains and provides safe monitoring environment. The proposed camera’s cover lens consists of transparent electrode patterns and hydrophobic dielectric layers and it is fabricated by semiconductor manufacturing processes. To investigate the effect of the cover lens based on electrowetting actuation on droplet removal, the cleaning time and cleaning efficiency of droplets are measured using a high-speed camera. To validate the applicability of the self-cleaning camera, the self-cleaning technology of the camera is demonstrated on droplets formed on the cover lens surface of the camera. The demonstration shows that the camera image distorted by droplets that occur on the initial cover lens is quickly restored by electrowetting actuation. The proposed surveillance camera can promptly remove droplets on the surface of the cover lens. Thus, it can be applied not only for the military surveillance systems but also for security cameras for daily life safety and future industries such as smart-factory and smart-city.
