TI  - System for blockchain and Internet Of Things (IOT)            based secure future city architecture, has unique            architecture that is utilized to resist incorporating            blockchain technologies into IOT devices such that wide            range of IOT situations is provided with minimal            functionality
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has an architecture which connects                the geographically dispersed sensor networks to a                decentralized access control scheme. The system is                built on blockchain technologies, and enforces                access control policies. The unique architecture is                utilized to resist incorporating blockchain                technologies into IOT devices. The wide range of                IOT situations is provided with minimal                functionality.
                    USE - System for blockchain and Internet Of Things                (IOT) based secure future city architecture used in                many areas of modern economy such as facilities for                manufacturing, utilities, distribution, recreation,                military, residential, commercial, and                healthcare.
                    ADVANTAGE - The IOT is the developmental innovation that                has filled in ubiquity in science and designing                applications to tackle difficulties without the                requirement for human impedance. The IOT is                integrated into a variety of industries to provide                a more cognitive framework for providing                personalized applications to consumers such that                the overall experience is improved. The blockchain                and distributed ledger technologies have the                potential to solve the scalability, trust,                security, and privacy problems that IOT and smart                city applications encounter. The most                cost-effective approach to use blockchain based                safety clarifications and developing a mechanism                can ensure the safety and secrecy of applications                in blockchain. The blockchain technology has the                ability to be immensely helpful in ensuring                trustworthy and accurate data such that the                big-data innovations are allowed to reach the                maximum potential and develop innovative solutions                focused on healthcare data. The stakeholders in the                supply chain can use blockchain to more efficiently                control the movement of resources and products from                different points in the network, and can improve                the protection of IOT devices in use and promote                due diligence. The highly observable supply chain                is a good way to reduce knowledge asymmetry,                uncertainties, and organizational inefficiencies in                smart cities. The blockchain helps smart city                growth by improving the efficiency of supply chains                and the quality and traceability of goods during                the manufacturing and usage cycles. The blockchain                technology enables smart city residents to monitor                and trace the origins of their goods and services                such that the customer loyalty and confidence can                be increased. Smart mobility increases the                accessibility and affordability of new and                environmentally friendly transportation services.                Smart mobility necessitates the implementation of                cost-effective, environmentally friendly, and                sustainable public transportation. The smart-city                planners can use blockchain to build an efficient                transit network that allows people to check for and                pay for services directly. The efficiency of public                transit can be improved with smart mobility systems                built on the blockchain. The citizens in smart                cities will benefit from blockchain technologies by                having easier connections to public transit,                shorter travel times, and increased safety. The                public transit services and private mobility                providers can use blockchain technologies to                minimize emissions, lower costs, boost sales, and                improve customer loyalty. The blockchain technology                enables smart cities public governance to be more                efficient and transparent, and has the ability to                boost community interest in government. The                blockchain has potential to allow the government to                provide people with more customized services while                still increasing transparency. The blockchain                technology allows e-voting to enhance efficiency,                to lower costs, and to guarantee a fair and                inclusive voting process.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows the schematic diagram                illustrating the data flow architecture in                Blockchain integrated IOT architecture.
