TI  - Method for smart mobility and traffic management            through wireless sensor networks in sectors, such as            smart cities, involves investigating and simulating            application of Dijkstra algorithm, Bellman Ford            algorithm and Floyd-Warshall algorithm for routing in            wireless sensor networks
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves investigating and                simulating the application of Dijkstra algorithm,                Bellman Ford algorithm and Floyd-Warshall algorithm                for routing in wireless sensor networks. The                simulations are conducted using the CupCarbon U-one                4.2 simulator. The simulation is carried out for                different sizes of the network. The techniques are                implemented to interact with vehicles or mobile                nodes and guide them to follow the shortest route                with less traffic. The sensor nodes detect the                vehicles or mobile nodes and assign a unique                identification to keep track of the vehicles.
                    USE - Method for smart mobility and traffic                management through wireless sensor networks in                sectors, such as military, healthcare, industry,                agriculture, livestock farming and smart                cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables analyzing the simulation                results to assess the performance of each algorithm                in the context of wireless sensor networks for                computing the shortest route from source to                destination, hence providing a robust solution for                dynamic and unpredictable scenarios in smart                mobility, intelligent accident management, and                efficient traffic management.
