TI  - Mesh route selection method based on graph neural            network and reinforcement learning for use in smart            city, involves using graph neural network to extract            embedded representation of each router node, and            defining multi-target reward function for guiding            Q-learning training process
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves constructing (S1) a mesh                network graph structure model. The graph neural                network is used to extract the embedded                representation of each router node. A route                decision mechanism is designed based on Q-learning                and combining the current router node state and the                neighbor information to generate a Q value. The                Masking mechanism is introduced to process the                dynamic action space, and shielding the illegal                next jump action. A multi-target reward function is                defined for guiding the Q-learning training                process.
                    USE - Mesh route selection method based on graph                neural network and reinforcement learning for use                in smart city, industrial automation and military                communication.
                    ADVANTAGE - The mesh route selecting method solves the                problems of poor adaptive capacity to dynamic                network environment, low route efficiency and lack                of intelligent decision support in the current                technology, and improves the data transmission                performance of the mesh network.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating                the mesh route selection method based on graph                neural network and reinforcement learning for use                in smart city (Drawing includes non-English                language text).S1Step for constructing a mesh network graph                structure modelS2Step for using the graph neural network to                extract the embedded representation of each router                nodeS3Step for designing a route decision                mechanism based on Q-learning and combining the                current router node state and the neighbour                information to generate a Q valueS4Step for introducing the Masking mechanism                to process the dynamic action space, and shielding                the illegal next jump actionS5Step for defining a multi-target reward                function for guiding the Q-learning training                process
