TI  - Pedestrian re-identification video stream complex            target detection method based on event-related            potential used in smart city, involves inputting            electroencephalogram signal into model after training,            detecting whether complex target appears, and appearing            and disappearing time of target
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves using (S1) a fast sequence                vision in a brain-computer interface to present an                experiment mode. Brain wave data is collected (S2)                when the experiment mode is tested.                Electroencephalogram data is filtered. A signal is                intercepted when there is no target. Three types of                samples of no target sample, a target appearing                sample and a target disappearing sample are                obtained (S3). The samples of the same type are                combined in pairs to form a positive sample pair. A                distance of characteristic vectors of two samples                in a sample pair is calculated (S4) on a same                vector space. An electroencephalogram signal is                obtained when a video stream is to be tested. The                electroencephalogram signal is input (S5) into a                model after training. Determination is made to                check (S6) whether a complex target appears and,                appearing and disappearing time of target.
                    USE - Pedestrian re-identification video stream                complex target detection method based on                event-related potential used in smart city and                military security.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables solving extreme class                imbalance problem of the sample in the video model                and distinguishing problem between two similar                classes using circle loss for reverse propagation,                and updating model parameters such that distance                between two samples in the positive sample pair is                closer and distance between the two samples is                closer in the negative sample pair, so that a                trained model is used to judge whether the target                appears in a video stream, and the appearing and                disappearing time of the target.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for                computer-readable storage medium comprising a set                of instructions for pedestrian re-identification                video stream complex target detection method based                on event-related potential.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating                the pedestrian re-identification video stream                complex target detection method based on                event-related potential used in smart city (Drawing                includes non-English language text).
