TI  - Robust distributed cooperative positioning method            for mobile unmanned system used in civil field e.g.            smart city, involves using alternative estimation            method of agent state and hidden variable for combined            posterior distribution to realize distributed location            of mobile unmanned system
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves introducing ((1)) the                global navigation satellite system (GNSS) hidden                variable in the GNSS observation model. The natural                function is obtained, where the GNSS hidden                variable comprises unknown GNSS pseudo-range                measurement deviation and unknown GNSS measurement                noise precision. An ultra-wideband (UWB) hidden                variable is introduced in UWB observation model.                The natural function is obtained, where the UWB                hidden variable comprises unknown observation                deviation and unknown UWB distance measuring noise                precision. The GNSS hidden variable and the UWB                hidden variable are modeled ((2)). The joint                posterior distribution of all vehicles and hidden                variable is established ((3)) as the distributed                cooperative locating problem target function based                on the hidden variable model. The alternative                estimation method of the agent state and the hidden                variable for the combined posterior distribution is                used ((4)) to realize the distributed location of                the mobile unmanned system.
                    USE - Robust distributed cooperative positioning                method for mobile unmanned system used in civil and                military fields such as smart city, transportation                and rescue.
                    ADVANTAGE - The combined posterior distribution adopts the                alternative estimation method of the agent state                and the hidden variable to realize the distributed                location of the mobile unmanned system.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram illustrating                the robust distributed cooperative positioning                method for mobile unmanned system. (Drawing                includes non-English language text)(1)Step for introducing GNSS hidden variable                in GNSS observation model(2)Step for modeling GNSS hidden variable and                UWB hidden variable(3)Step for establishing joint posterior                distribution of all vehicles and hidden variable as                distributed cooperative locating problem target                function based on hidden variable model(4)Step for using alternative estimation                method of agent state and hidden variable for                combined posterior distribution to realize                distributed location of mobile unmanned                system
