TI  - Computing device for locating object in            operational area, has display device that displays            graphic of operational area and position of composite            two-dimensional shape of object within the operational            area is determined by selected vector segment
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The device has a processing device for                generating a graphic of an operational area by                extracting vector data and attributes of each                two-dimensional shape of an object from a set of                data streams. The processing device identifies                vector pairs from the vector data, and calculates                mutually-normal vector segments between the vector                pairs. A display device (118) displays the graphic                of the operational area, where a position of the                composite two-dimensional shape of the object is                determined within the area by a selected vector                segment. The vector segments are selected according                to predetermined pattern recognition criteria                associated with the detected object.
                    USE - Computing device for locating object in                operational area, such as military base, airport,                stadium, transit system, smart city, power plant or                detention facility.
                    ADVANTAGE - The computing device comprises a receiving                device that is connected to a network, where                processing device is configured to generate a                graphic of the operational area by extracting                vector data and attributes of each two dimensional                shape of the object from multiple data streams, and                thus enables to maintain situational awareness of a                force protection area to mitigate hostile actions                against military personnel, the general public,                resources, facilities and critical infrastructure,                such as a military base, airport, stadium, transit                system, smart city, power plant or detention                facility, and autonomously react to newly sensed                information in the locations.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for:(1) a method for locating an object in an                operational area;(2) a method for determining a location of an                object;(3) an edge device in a network for locating                an object in an operational area;(4) a system with image sensors configured to                capture video data of an object.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic diagram of the                computing device for locating object in operational                area.111Image sensor112Central processing unit115Memory device116Transmit or receive device118Display device
