TI  - Smart recognition system for armed threats, has            pose estimation module that analyzes key points and            postures of individuals, threat classification module            that ascribes levels of risk depending on weapon            presence and posture, and alert generation interface            that alerts operators in real time
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a real-time video acquisition                module for capturing live feed, and an object                detection module using deep learning-based object                detection frameworks for detecting firearms. A pose                estimation module analyzes key points and postures                of individuals, and a threat classification module                ascribes levels of risk depending on weapon                presence and posture. An alert generation interface                alerts operators in real time. The firearm                detection is conducted by YOLO or similar onestage                deep learning based detection models. The framework                is deployable for public safety, law enforcement,                defense, and smart city infrastructure.
                    USE - Smart recognition system for armed threats.                Uses include but are not limited to public safety                infrastructures, airports, schools, military                installations, and smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system realizes fusion of weapon detection                with the analysis of human posture that guarantees                that the threat is recognized by the visible                presence of weapons and by intent expressed through                body language, which makes the system more                intelligent, quicker, and more accurate for                deployment in reality. The system is a real-time                deep learning-powered system to identify firearms                accurately and detect armed threats through                inspection of both object presence and human                posture. The system minimizes false positives by                incorporating pose estimation methods that                differentiate benign firearm carry from threatening                postures such as aiming, raising, or pointing a                gun. The system introduces contextual realization                of human behavior, thus allowing for accurate                realtime threat detection.
