TI  - Method for wireless communication, involves using            second indication information for indicating whether            site device requests to obtain enhanced distributed            channel access (EDCA) parameter set
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves sending a first request                frame to the first access point device by the                station device. The first request frame includes                first indication information and or second                indication information. The first indication                information is used to indicate whether the site                device requests a first access point device (AA) to                transfer the national security and emergency                preparedness (NSEP) priority access permission                information of the site device to a second access                point device (BB). The second indication                information is used to indicate whether the site                device requests to obtain an enhanced distributed                channel access (EDCA) parameter set. The first                access point device is an access point device                currently associated with the site device. The                second AP device is a target AP device to be                associated with the station device.
                    USE - Method for wireless communication for site                device e.g. mobile phone, flat computer (Pad), with                wireless transceiver function of computer, virtual                reality (VR) device, augmented reality (AR) device,                wireless device in industrial control, wireless                device in unmanned (self-driving), wireless device                in remote medical, wireless device in smart grid,                wireless device in transportation safety, smart                city wireless device or wireless device in smart                home in smart city, and access point device (all                claimed) used in communication systems e.g.                wireless local area networks (WLAN), and wireless                fidelity (Wi-Fi).
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables the station device current                associated access point device to transfer the NSEP                priority access permission information of the                device to the target device in the process of                station device switching AP, thus reducing the                switching overhead, and reducing the time delay of                the priority access service. The method allows the                authorized user to use system resource                preferentially, thus improving the probability of                successful communication under the network                congestion condition, and hence improving the                quality of service (QoS) of the wireless                communication.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:a site device;an access point device;a chip;a computer readable storage medium storing                program for wireless communication;a computer program product for wireless                communication; anda computer program for wireless                communication.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram of method                for wireless communication. (Drawing includes                non-English language text)AAFirst access point deviceBBSecond access point deviceS210Step for sending the NSEP priority access                permission information of the site device to the                second access point device by the first access                point device, and the first access point device is                an access point device currently associated with                the site device, and the second access point device                is a target access point device to be associated                with the site device
