TI  - Face coordinate system conversion method of full            spatial information system applied to satellite            positioning and navigation, involves using plug-in            design to realize extension of spatial reference            system
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves calculating relative state                refers to a nine-degree-of-freedom spatial                reference tree. Iterative calculation and                coordinate conversion are required in relative                spatial state query calculation according to the                parent-child node relationship in                nine-degree-of-freedom spatial reference tree. The                plug-in design and implementation are referred to                designing a spatial reference system and a                converter. The plug-in design is used to realize                the extension of the spatial reference                system.
                    USE - Face coordinate system conversion method of                full spatial information system applied to                satellite positioning and navigation, aerospace                remote sensing, smart cities, territorial planning                and military applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The calculation precision and calculation                efficiency are improved. The accuracy and                reliability of the coordinate conversion are                improved. The good extensibility and implementation                efficiency are achieved.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of the                coordinate system frame of the full spatial                information system. (Drawing includes non-English                language text)
