TI  - Real-time building detection and segmentation            system, has residual and involutional layer-enhanced            U-Net based Generative Adversarial Network model for            building segmentation, where Raspberry Pi IoT module            realizes real-time inference and deployment
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a residual and involutional                layer-enhanced U-Net based Generative Adversarial                Network (GAN) model for building segmentation. A                Raspberry Pi IoT module realizes real-time                inference and deployment. An aerial drone platform                is coupled with the IoT system for real-time data                capture and remote monitoring, where the U-Net                model uses residual learning to enhance feature                extraction, preserve gradient flow, and reduce                vanishing gradient problems during deep network                training. An involutional layer is used to provide                adaptive spatial filtering with channel-wise weight                sharing for facilitating spatially variant                processing and increasing model efficiency for edge                deployment.
                    USE - Real-time building detection and segmentation                system for use in applications. Uses include but                are not limited to smart city planning,                post-disaster damage analysis, environmental                monitoring and military surveillance.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system integrates GAN-enhanced U-Net model                with Raspberry Piand drones, thus providing a                compact, cost-effective, and deployable solution                for real-time building detection from satellite and                drone imagery.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a                real-time building detection and segmentation                system.
