TI  - Robust collaborative positioning method for            multi-epoch observation correlation under model            mismatch used in smart city, involves using            Gauss-Wishart distribution to model hidden variable,            and estimating marginal posterior of each agent state            and marginal posterior of hidden variable
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves constructing (1)                measurement bias hidden variables and measurement                noise hidden variables to characterize the bias and                noise of multi-epoch observations by observation                model modeling. The agent state of the historical                epoch is inferred (2) using the kinematic model of                agent from epoch t-1 to epoch t, and the                observation model is substituted into the                observation model and the observation association                is performed for a period of time to obtain                multi-epoch observation model by correlation of                observation quantity of multiple epochs. The                Gauss-Wishart distribution is used (3) to model                hidden variables and hidden variable distribution                is obtained by observing hidden variable modeling.                The marginal posterior of each agent state and the                marginal posterior of the hidden variable are                simultaneously estimated (4) to achieve robust                collaborative positioning by distributed robust                positioning according to the multi-epoch                observation model and hidden variable                distribution.
                    USE - Robust collaborative positioning method for                multi-epoch observation correlation under model                mismatch for multi-agent system (MAS), including                Unmanned Ground Vehicles (UGVs), unmanned Aerial                Vehicles (UAVs), multi-robots, etc., has been                widely used in civil and military fields such as                smart cities, transportation, and rescue.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method constrains the state of the agent                that changes over time through the state transfer                equation, and introduces hidden variables to                characterize the deviation and noise of multi-epoch                observations, to eliminate the observation                deviation caused by the non-adaptation of the                observation model and the deterioration of                positioning performance, and enhance the robustness                of positioning.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block flow diagram                illustrating the robust collaborative positioning                method for multi-epoch observation correlation                under model mismatch. (Drawing includes non-English                language text)1Step for constructing measurement bias                hidden variables and measurement noise hidden                variables2Step for inferring the agent state of the                historical epoch using the kinematic model of the                agent from epoch t-1 to epoch t3Step for using Gauss-Wishart distribution to                model hidden variables4Step for estimating the marginal posterior                of each agent state and the marginal posterior of                the hidden variable
