TI  - Method for providing optimized cluster formation            using unsupervised k-means algorithm, involves            optimizing cluster formation using an unsupervised            k-means algorithm to ensure more effective cluster head            selection
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves optimizing cluster                formation using an unsupervised k-means algorithm                to ensure more effective cluster head selection by                considering essential parameters like distance to                the control center, residual energy, and mobility,                instead of relying on random probability. A single                optimal path and forward node (104) is identified                based on residual energy. The proposed approach                decreases energy consumption in network nodes by                limiting unnecessary communication between the base                station and network nodes.
                    USE - Method for providing optimized cluster                formation using unsupervised k-means algorithm for                use in environmental monitoring, healthcare,                military surveillance, smart city infrastructures                and agricultural management.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables providing efficient data                transmission strategies for prolonging network                lifetime and ensuring reliable communication, thus                improving efficiency and reducing latency in                wireless sensor networks (WSNs) and reducing energy                consumption for nodes closer to a base                station.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a system                for providing optimized cluster formation using                unsupervised k-means algorithm.101Node placement algorithm102Cluster formation algorithm104Node109RBCMIC115Machine learning algorithm
