TI  - Smart defense system for improving cyber security            in wireless sensor networks using artificial            intelligence, has wireless sensor nodes deployed across            network and configured to collect real time            environmental data
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system uses artificial intelligence (AI)                to detect multiple types of intrusions in real                time. An AI model classifies threats including DoS,                Sybil, and wormhole attacks. Features including                packet loss, energy use, and node behavior are                extracted for detection. The AI model updates                continuously to adapt to intrusion patterns. The                automated responses include isolating nodes and                alerting administrators. The architecture supports                flat and hierarchical wireless sensor network (WSN)                topologies. The secure communication ensures data                integrity during attacks.
                    USE - Smart defense system for wireless sensor                networks using AI to detect multiple types of                intrusions in real time for applications. Uses                include but are not limited to military security,                health monitoring, smart cities, industrial                automation, military surveillance, and                environmental monitoring applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system delivers high detection accuracy                and reduces false positives, ensuring smooth                network operations. The system uses optimized AI                algorithms that work with minimal power and                processing resources, thus ensuring continuous                monitoring without affecting network performance.                The system is a robust and scalable solution for                safeguarding wireless sensor networks, offering                real-time threat detection, automated responses,                and efficient operation in low-power                environments.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                method for detecting multiple types of intrusions                in real time.
