TI  - Vehicle underbody inspection system for detecting            hidden objects beneath vehicles in real time, has            artificial intelligence powered sensors and 360-degree            cameras for advanced monitoring, and providing instant            alerts drivers via advanced driver assistance systems            and mobile applications
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has artificial intelligence (AI)                powered sensors and 360-degree cameras for advanced                monitoring, and providing instant alerts drivers                via advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS) and                mobile applications. The system improves security                by identifying unauthorized modifications or                foreign objects. The system realizes software                components image processing, anomaly detection                algorithms, AI and machine learning, pattern                recognition systems integration, and ADAS                interfaces.
                    USE - Vehicle underbody inspection system (VUIS) for                detecting hidden objects, obstacles, and living                beings beneath vehicles in real time. Uses include                but are not limited to smart cities, military                checkpoints, high-security zones, and commercial                transportation.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system improves road safety, enhances                security measures at checkpoints, car parks , and                high-risk areas, while preventing unauthorized                objects or threats from being concealed under                vehicles. The system leverages cutting-edge AI,                internet of things (IoT), and cloud-based data                processing to revolutionize the automotive industry                and support the advancement of Level 5 autonomous                vehicles, making roads safer and smarter. The                system provides instant alerts through mobile                applications and vehicle dashboards, thus ensuring                that drivers can take necessary precautions before                movement.
