TI  - Method for testing semiconductor on-chip direct            current based on bias device, involves judging working            condition of tested semiconductor according to change            condition of drain current, and performing direct            current test
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves connecting a drain power                supply loop serially with a bias device, where the                bias device is close to a position of a tested                semiconductor. A capacitor is connected with the                semiconductor in parallel manner. A probe is added                on a welding disk at two ends of a grid electrode                and a drain electrode in a feeding way. The grid                voltage and the drain voltage are adjusted. A                change condition of drain current is observed. A                working condition of the semiconducting                semiconductor is determined according to the change                condition of the drain current. A direct current                test is performed when the semiconductor is working                normally.
                    USE - Method for testing semiconductor on-chip                direct current based on bias device for                semiconductor devices and chips used in military                equipment, electronic warfare, intelligent                communication technology, intelligent household and                smart city.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method eliminates the power ripple                avoiding low frequency oscillation of the device in                the test process, and improves the test accuracy,                research and application of device electric                characteristics.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic diagram of a                method for testing semiconductor on-chip direct                current based on bias device (Drawing includes                non-English language text).
