TI  - Method for detecting black hole and flooding            attacks in wireless sensor network, involves collecting            real-time network traffic data, extracting features            from data, and applying trained machine learning model            to classify node behavior as normal or malicious
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves collecting real-time                network traffic data, extracting features from                data, and applying a trained machine learning model                to classify node behavior as normal or malicious.                The machine learning model is provided with random                forest, K-nearest neighbors (KNN), decision trees,                or autoencoders.
                    USE - Method for detecting black hole and flooding                attacks in wireless sensor network in critical                domains such as military surveillance,                environmental monitoring, healthcare and smart                cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method uses machine learning for smarter                and faster detection.The method handles two major                types of attacks together, not just one. The method                is designed to work well even on low-power sensor                devices. The method adapts to new threats over time                by learning from experience. The method                automatically blocks harmful nodes and alert others                without human help.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:(1) a system for detecting black hole and                flooding attacks in wireless sensor network;                and(2) a real-time mitigation mechanism.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a                machine learning driven advanced defence mechanisms                against black hole and flooding attacks in wireless                sensor networks.
