TI  - Method for providing secure, energy-efficient            wireless sensor network communication for e.g. military            surveillance applications, involves using combined            trust evaluation and energy-aware clustering/routing to            perform cluster head selection
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves using combined trust                evaluation and energy-aware clustering/routing to                perform cluster head selection and prioritize nodes                with high trust scores arid sufficient energy.                Routing decisions balance energy consumption and                security. A dynamic cluster updating adapts to                topology changes against selective forwarding and                sinkhole attacks. Simulation validation                demonstrates superior performance in real-time                wireless sensor network applications.
                    USE - Method for providing secure, energy-efficient                wireless sensor network communication using                combined trust evaluation and energy-aware                clustering/routing protocols. Uses include but are                not limited to military surveillance applications,                industrial automation applications, healthcare                monitoring applications, environmental data                collection applications and smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables enhancing packet delivery                ratio, reducing communication overhead, and                improving fault tolerance and robustness of the                network so as to enhance data integrity,                confidentiality, node reliability, and efficient                energy usage during communication in networks. The                method enbles ensuring that trustworthy and                energy-efficient nodes are given key communication                roles so as to reduce risk of data compromise, node                failures, and premature energy depletion, thus                extending overall lifetime and stability of the                wireless sensor network.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a system                for providing secure, energy-efficient wireless                sensor network communication using combined trust                evaluation and energy-aware clustering/routing                protocols.
