TI  - Multi-mode combined up-conversion frequency            environment vibrating energy collector used in sensor,            has piezoelectric energy capture unit which is located            between electromagnetic energy capture unit and            electrostatic energy capture unit
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The collector has low frequency vibration beam                (2) and high frequency beam (3) which are connected                to the casing (1). The low frequency vibration beam                is located above the high frequency beam. The low                frequency vibration beam is connected to the                electromagnetic energy capture unit (5). The                piezoelectric energy capture unit (8) and the                electrostatic energy capture unit (10) share the                high frequency beam. The electrostatic energy                capture unit is located at the lowest layer of the                casing. The piezoelectric energy capture unit is                located between the electromagnetic energy capture                unit and the electrostatic energy capture                unit.
                    USE - Multi-mode combined up-conversion frequency                environment vibrating energy collector used for                powering micro-electromechanical system (MEMS)                sensor in wireless sensor networks used in defense                military, smart city, intelligent manufacturing,                automatic driving, and environmental                protection.
