TI  - System for dynamically reducing power consumption            of low-power integrated circuit design for wireless            sensor networks, has sensor interface module, low-power            processor core, context-aware power control unit and            sleep/wake controller connected together
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a sensor interface module, a                low-power processor core, a context-aware power                control unit (CAPCU) and a sleep/wake controller                connected together. A system body dynamically                adjusts power consumption based on workload and                environmental conditions. A processor core supports                dynamic voltage and frequency scaling (DVFS) to                adjust clock frequency and voltage based on current                workload. The CAPCU uses machine learning                algorithms to predict future energy requirements                based on historical energy usage patterns and                real-time environmental data. The controller                transitions the system between active, idle and                deep sleep states.
                    USE - System for dynamically reducing power                consumption of low-power IC in wireless sensor                networks (WSNs) of various applications. Uses                include but are not limited to environmental                monitoring, healthcare systems, military                surveillance, and smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system achieves significant reductions in                power consumption while maintaining high                performance levels for real-time applications by                leveraging a combination of dynamic voltage and                frequency scaling (DVFS), sub-threshold operation,                and predictive machine learning-based power                control. The system reduces dynamic power                consumption by a factor of approximately 4 to 6                compared to normal operation without introducing                significant performance degradation for many sensor                tasks. The system allows WSN nodes to operate                efficiently for extended periods and enhances                sustainability and practicality of systems.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                method for dynamically reducing power consumption                of low-power integrated circuits.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a system                for dynamically reducing power consumption of                low-power IC in WSN.
