AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a memory storing                machine-readable instructions that causes a                processor to process past agent-trajectory data                (240), map data (116), and sensor data (245) using                encoder neural networks to produce combined encoded                input data. The processor generates a weights                vector for a Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM) based on                the combined encoded input data, produces                volumetric spatio-temporal representation of                occupancy in an environment of a robot by                generating corresponding sample probability                distributions of scene occupancy based on                respective means and variances of modes for modes                of the GMM in accordance with the weights vector,                where the respective means and variances sample                coefficients of a set of learned basis functions.                The processor controls operation of the robot based                on the volumetric spatio-temporal representation of                occupancy.
