AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method (500) involves receiving (520) a                request to build a backup directed acyclic graph                (BDAG) of backup devices for routing traffic within                the computer network in case of a power outage at a                device of computer network. The request comprises                requirement specifying to use a device remaining                powered after power outage as a backup device. A                set of backup devices fulfilling the requirement is                identified (530) in response to receiving the                request. A backup device is selected (540) and is                synchronized (550) with the device of computer                network according to backup operation                strategy.
                    USE - Method for pre-computation of backup                topologies in computer networks such as wide area                networks, sensor networks, Low power and Lossy                Networks (LLNs) for military applications. Uses                include but are not limited to monitor physical or                environmental conditions, and to connect lights,                appliances, vehicles, heating, ventilating, and                air-conditioning (HVAC), windows, shades and                blinds, doors, locks, used in smart grid, smart                cities, building and industrial automation                applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method for pre-computation of backup                topologies in computer networks leads to faster                convergence time as well as maintaining the quality                of service for the traffic during power outage. The                individual backup operation strategy is refined to                increase the robustness of the backup directed                acyclic graph in the event of power outage.
