TI  - Fuzzy logic-based routing system for flying ad hoc            network, has fuzzy rule base for evaluating link            conditions and enabling congestion-resilient routing,            where congestion is detected based on fuzzy            thresholds
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system integrates congestion control                mechanisms. The routing decisions are based on                fuzzy evaluation of speed, signal strength, and                queue length. The congestion is detected based on                fuzzy thresholds, and triggers load balancing                mechanisms. A real-time congestion detection                algorithm is implemented using Mamdani fuzzy                inference model on embedded unmanned aerial vehicle                (UAV) hardware. A framework is provided for                reducing packet loss and delay in FANETs using                adaptive route selection informed by fuzzy metrics.                The routes are dynamically selected based on fuzzy                logic cost functions that minimize congestion and                maximize reliability.
                    USE - Fuzzy logic-based routing system for FANETs                for mission-critical applications e.g. disaster                response, military surveillance, environmental                monitoring, and smart city infrastructure.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables providing a routing system                that incorporates real-time decision-making                capabilities using intelligent techniques including                fuzzy logic to provide congestion control and                enhance quality of service by intelligently                adjusting the routing based on environmental and                network parameters, thus maintaining communication                links, reducing unnecessary transmissions,                balancing traffic load, and ultimately improving                quality of service metrics e.g. latency,                throughput, and packet delivery ratio, and hence                minimizing energy consumption, and extending                network lifetime.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included for: (1)                a method for maintaining quality of service in                FANETs using a fuzzy-enhanced AODV routing                protocol; (2) a UAV communication system; (3) a                real-time congestion detection algorithm; (4) a                framework for reducing packet loss and delay in                FANETs using adaptive route selection informed by                fuzzy metrics.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic view of a Fuzzy                logic-based routing system.
