TI  - Trust-aware secure routing protocol for wireless            sensor networks (WSNs) using hybrid firebug optimized            modified bee colony (FOMBC) algorithm, computes trust            values for each node based on packet forwarding            behavior to mitigate grey-hole and black-hole            attacks
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The protocol computes the trust values for                each node based on packet forwarding behavior to                mitigate grey-hole and black-hole attacks. The                firebug optimization (FBO) is employed to enhance                global exploration and modified bee colony (MBC) to                refine local optimization for route selection. A                multi-objective fitness function is used combining                trust value, connectivity, quality of service (QoS)                metrics, and distance. The higher throughput,                reduced latency, and improved packet delivery ratio                are achieved over traditional protocols such as                simple opportunistic adaptive routing (SOAR).
                    USE - Trust-aware secure routing protocol for                wireless sensor networks (WSNs) using hybrid                firebug optimized modified bee colony (FOMBC)                algorithm for use in real-time WSN applications                such as military defense, healthcare monitoring,                smart cities, and industrial automation (all                claimed).
                    ADVANTAGE - The secure and energy-efficient routing                protocol combines intelligence and trust evaluation                to enhance data transmission reliability and                resistance to attacks in distributed sensor                networks. The trust-aware routing protocol is                developed that enhances security in WSNs. The event                black-hole and grey-hole attacks through dynamic                trust evaluation are improved. The packet delivery                ratio is improved, latency is reduced, and the                energy usage is optimized. The firebug optimization                (FBO) and modified bee colony (MBC) are integrated                for intelligent path selection. The adaptive                fitness function is provided that balances trust,                connectivity, QoS, and distance. The scalable                routing solution offers for real-time applications                in sensitive domains such as defense and                healthcare.
