TI  - System for managing devices in communication            network implemented at premises, has server that            processes first output and second output using            reinforcement learning-based processing loop to            determine action that is to be implemented for managing            devices in communication network
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has a server (112) which is                configured to obtain premises planning data and                network data from a service associated with the                premises (110). The premises planning data pertains                to floor plan of the premises and the network data                pertains to the devices in the communication                network and a performance of the communication                network. The devices in the communication network                are communicably/operably coupled in a mesh network                topology. The server is configured to process the                premises planning data through a first processing                pipeline to generate a first output. The server is                configured to process the network data through a                second processing pipeline to generate a second                output. The server is configured to process the                first output and the second output using a                reinforcement learning-based processing loop to                determine action that is to be implemented for                managing the devices in the communication                network.
                    USE - System for managing devices in communication                network that is implemented at premises. Uses                include but are not limited to military                organizations, smart cities, industrial automation,                emergency services and agriculture.
                    ADVANTAGE - The mesh networks easily increases range by                connecting the nodes to gateways, where the                gateways transfer the messages to the other mesh                devices in the mesh network. The mesh network                reduces redundancy by configuring a given mesh                device to both receive and translate information                received from other mesh device.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:1. a method for managing devices; and2. a computer-program product storing program                for managing devices.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram                illustrating a system for managing devices in a                communication network.100System for managing devices in                communication network implemented at                premises102,104,106Devices110Premise112Server114Data repository
