TI  - Charging utility optimization-oriented            fine-grained power distribution method in Internet of            things (IOT) used in field of military, involves            solving wireless sensing network utility maximization            problem model, and determining power of each time slice            of charging station
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves constructing (S1) a                wireless sensing network model, where the wireless                sensing network model comprises a charging station                and a chargeable sensor. An effective energy                received is determined (S2) by a sensor requesting                charging in a charging period, and the utility sum                of the sensors requesting charging is determined                according to the effective energy. The utility sum                is converted (S3) into a wireless sensor network                utility maximization problem model under the double                constraints of the maximum off-duty time limit and                the charging cost limit of the sensor. The wireless                sensing network utility maximization problem model                is solved (S4), and the power of each time slice of                the charging station is determined to obtain a                power distribution strategy scheme.
                    USE - Charging utility optimization-oriented                fine-grained power distribution method in Internet                of things (IOT) used in field of military, disaster                early warning and smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The charging cost and the charging                effectiveness is balanced according to the                requirement, more flexible and efficient charging                service is provided, and the quality and the                efficiency of the whole network charging service                are improved.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a fine                grained power distribution system for optimizing                charging effect in internet of things.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow chart illustrating a                charging utility optimization-oriented fine-grained                power distribution method in the Internet of                things. (Drawing includes non-English language                text).S1Step for constructing a wireless sensing                network modelS2Step for determining effective energy                received by a sensor requesting charging in a                charging periodS3Step for converting the utility sum into a                wireless sensor network utility maximization                problem modelS4Step for solving the wireless sensing                network utility maximization problem model
