TI  - System for monitoring operational area, has            processor that generates signal encoded with data for            verifying three-dimensional virtual visualization of            operational area including prioritized operational            sub-regions
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has a communication interface                for communicating with a network (140), and a                memory device for storing a set of data streams. A                sensor transmits a data stream periodically or                non-periodically to a processor over the network,                or transmits data to the processor when a change in                a spatial characteristic of an operational                sub-region is detected. The sensor generates the                data streams by observing the operational area,                where a three dimensional geometry of each                operational sub region is determined based on                sensing characteristics of the sensor arrangement.                The 3D geometry is dimensioned according to spatial                properties of the operational region.
                    USE - Method for monitoring an operational area to                maintain situational awareness of a force                protection area to mitigate hostile actions against                military personnel, the general public, resources,                facilities and critical information. Uses include                but are not limited to military base, airport,                stadium, transit system, smart city, power plant or                detention facility.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method effectively monitors the                operational area in the network in a simple and                effective manner. The method allows the operator to                quickly make decisions by having the system                recommend predefined rules of engagement based on                the newly sensed situational awareness information,                and to support decision-making actions independent                of an operator if the automated responses are                properly controlled and potential consequences of                improper responses are carefully considered and the                associated potential risks are deemed to be                warranted.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included for the                following:a method for monitoring an operational area;                anda computer readable medium encoded with a                program for monitoring an operational area.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic diagram of the                system for dynamic three-dimensional command and                control.100System110Computing device119Database120Computing system140Network
