TI  - Method for identifying radio frequency fingerprint            small sample based on meta-learning model, involves            processing embedded function of support set, and            performing softmax normalization to obtain attention            kernel function calculation formula
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves making training sample,                (ii) randomly selecting k categories from the                obtained radio device I/Q signal, randomly                selecting s+ q samples for each category, (iii)                taking the k*s samples as the support set, (iv)                taking a k*q samples as a query set, taking a set                of support set and the query set as a training                task, taking all the training tasks needed in the                random sampling and obtaining S2, (v) constructing                a meta learning model, (vi) processing the embedded                function g of the support group, and (vii)                performing softmax normalization to obtain                attention kernel function calculation formula.                (viii) inputting the training sample set obtained                in step (a) to the meta- learning model constructed                in step S2 for training, (ix) embedding the feature                vector of the recognition task support group and                query.
                    USE - Method for identifying a radio frequency                fingerprint small sample based on meta-learning                model for intelligent home, internet of things,                vehicle networking, intelligent smart city and                other scenes in civil and military fields.
                    ADVANTAGE - The radio frequency fingerprint small sample                data set has good identification precision, and                avoids the model over-fitting problem caused by                data quantity.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating a                method for identifying a radio frequency                fingerprint small sample based on meta-learning                model (Drawing includes Non-English language                text).
