TI  - Charging scheduling method based on dynamic power            allocation in rechargeable wireless sensor network            (WSN) used in military monitoring field, involves            comparing obtained subsets to obtain optimal subset for            optimal charging scheduling strategy
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves maximizing the total                charging utility based on dynamic power allocation                in rechargeable WSN, and constructing an integer                programming model based on charging completion time                and charging service cost constraints. The network                model of the rechargeable WSN is established. The                target problem is transformed into equivalent                submodular function maximization problem based on                budget constraints by constructing non-negative and                monotonically non-decreasing submodular function.                The charging strategy of each charging station is                obtained using greedy strategy based on the                submodular function to obtain the final solution.                The largest subset of the corresponding submodular                function is obtained for the subset to satisfy the                budget constraint through the greedy strategy based                on the maximum marginal revenue value. The obtained                subsets are compared to obtain the optimal subset                for optimal charging scheduling strategy.
                    USE - Charging scheduling method based on dynamic                power allocation in rechargeable wireless sensor                network (WSN) used in military monitoring field,                disaster prediction field and smart city.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables realizing dynamic                distribution of charging power and corresponding                charging service time of each charging station, so                that total charging effectiveness obtained by all                sensor device is maximized, thus improving network                charging service quality and efficiency.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating                the charging scheduling process based on dynamic                power allocation in rechargeable WSN. (Drawing                includes non-English language text)
