TI  - Hybrid energy harvesting system for use in e.g.            smart buildings, has power management circuit            operatively connected to photovoltaic layer and            electrodes of plug-flow channels and storing and            regulating electrical energy from sources
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a set of electrodes positioned                within or adjacent to plug-flow channels for                harvesting electrical energy generated by kinetic                motion and dielectric separation of water slugs and                air. A raindrop capture and guiding mechanism                comprises surface microstructures or grooves for                channeling raindrops into the plug- flow channels.                A power management circuit is operatively connected                to a photovoltaic layer and the electrodes, and                stores and regulates the electrical energy from                sources, where the system operates in dry and rainy                conditions to enable continuous renewable                electricity generation. The flow channels are                formed using transparent polymeric materials                selected from a group consisting of                polydimethylsiloxane (PDMS), poly (methyl                methacrylate) (PMMA), fluoropolymers, or                hydrophobic composites.
                    USE - Hybrid energy rain-solar smart panel                harvesting system for use in applications. Uses                include but are not limited to smart buildings,                self-powered infrastructure, electric vehicle                stations, disaster-resilient shelters, remote rural                electrification systems, urban rooftops and green                buildings remote rural electrification, military or                emergency response shelters, internet-of-things                (IoT) devices and weather stations.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system combines photovoltaic energy                conversion with plug-flow or triboelectric                microchannel systems, thus enabling efficient and                uninterrupted energy production during dry and wet                weather conditions. The system utilizes a dual-mode                energy harvesting mechanism to enable reliable and                uninterrupted power generation for smart city                applications, off-grid installations, and                weather-variable environments. The system operates                in the dry and rainy conditions, thus enabling                continuous renewable electricity generation. The                system integrates solar photovoltaic (PV)                technology with a plug-flow microchannel based                raindrop energy converter, thus enabling continuous                and weather-adaptive power generation.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                method for continuous renewable energy                harvesting.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic view of a                system architecture with a layered design.
