TI  - Method for determining shortest route between            source node and destination node in wireless sensor            network for smart mobility applications, involves            analyzing simulation results indicating that            computation time for determining shortest routes            remains consistent, to ensure suitability for            applications
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves employing Dijkstra's                algorithm, Bellman-Ford algorithm, and                Floyd-Warshall algorithm to compute shortest routes                within a network. Simulations are conducted using a                CupCarbon U-One 4.2 simulator for networks of                varying sizes. Unique identifiers are assigned to                each sensor node to facilitate vehicle or mobile                node tracking. Interaction techniques are                implemented to guide vehicles or mobile nodes to                the shortest routes with minimal traffic.                Simulation results indicating that the computation                time for determining the shortest routes remains                consistent across all three algorithms, are                analyzed to ensure suitability for smart mobility                applications.
                    USE - Method for determining a shortest route                between a source node and a destination node in                wireless sensor network (WSN) for smart mobility                applications such as smart exit, efficient accident                management, smart accident management, smart van in                hazardous environment and smart traffic management                applications in smart cities. Can also be used in                military, healthcare, industry, agriculture and                livestock farming applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method ensures that the nodes of the WSN                are distributed randomly across an area to perceive                the surroundings, gather data, and communicate                wirelessly with the neighboring nodes and remote                users via the internet. The method also ensures                that all the data collected by sensors are sent to                access points at the roadside which can further                send warnings to the vehicle drivers to react                safely. The method enables sending the data to                vehicles by using the shortest routes to avoid time                delay.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic illustration of                simulation of Dijkstra algorithm within a CupCarbon                U-one 4.2 environment.
