TI  - Self-configuring ad hoc network system for            emergency communication in e.g. military operation, has            wireless nodes for autonomously establishing            communication links and forming network without manual            configuration, where nodes utilize adaptive routing            protocol
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a set of wireless nodes to                autonomously establish communication links and form                a network without manual configuration. The nodes                utilize an adaptive routing protocol to select the                most efficient communication path based on                real-time environmental conditions, where the nodes                dynamically adjust transmission power to optimize                energy efficiency and extend battery life. The                network supports multi-mode communication e.g.                text, voice, and data transmission, and the nodes                have modular hardware components to enable                customization based on application requirements.                The system incorporates secure encryption protocols                to prevent unauthorized access and interoperability                with existing emergency communication                systems.
                    USE - Self-configuring ad hoc network system for                emergency communication in situations for civilian                applications e.g. outdoor expeditions, rural                communication networks and smart city deployments.                Uses include but are not limited to natural                disasters, military operations, remote exploration,                and crisis scenarios.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system ensures dynamically adjusting to                changes in network topology, device mobility, and                environmental constraints without requiring human                intervention. The energy-efficient operation                mechanism allows each node to optimize power                consumption based on network conditions and                operational requirements. The system supports                multi-mode communication, thus enabling text,                voice, and data transmission over diverse frequency                bands, and hence enhancing versatility and                effectiveness across various emergency response                applications. The system includes a                self-configuring mechanism so as to ensure that                each node can automatically detect surroundings,                identify neighboring nodes, and establish                communication links accordingly.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included                for:a method for forming a self-configuring ad hoc                network;a method for ensuring network resilience in a                self-configuring ad hoc network.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a                self-configuring ad hoc network.
