TI  - Cyber-physical system for source location privacy            in wireless sensor network, has cyber-physical security            module that detects and mitigates adversarial attacks            raking source location privacy mechanism
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a source node that generates                event-based data packets for transmission through a                wireless sensor network (WSN). A privacy-preserving                routing mechanism obfuscates an actual source                location using active learning-based ensemble                classification. An ensemble classifier framework                includes multiple machine learning models trained                to distinguish routing anomalies and optimize the                obfuscation of the source location. An active                learning module selectively queries sensor nodes to                update the classifier dynamically based on                real-time network conditions. A cyber- physical                security module detects and mitigates adversarial                attacks raking the privacy mechanism of the                WSN.
                    USE - Enhanced cyber-physical system for source                location privacy based on active learning-based                ensemble classifier in WSNs in large geographical                areas to collect data for various applications.                Uses include but are not limited to environmental                monitoring, military surveillance, healthcare, and                smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system ensures combining the power of                active learning, ensemble machine learning                techniques, and privacy-preserving strategies, so                that the system offers a highly effective and                adaptable solution for ensuring the privacy of                sensor node locations, and maintain the efficiency                and scalability of large-scale networks. The system                protects sensitive data and enhances the overall                security and robustness of the system, thus making                the system suitable for a wide range of                applications where location privacy is paramount.                The system leverages active learning so as to                improve ability to detect and respond to new types                of attacks.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                method for enhancing source location privacy in a                wireless sensor network using an active                learning-based ensemble classifier.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow chart illustrating                an enhanced cyber-physical method for source                location privacy based on active learning-based                ensemble classifier in wireless sensor                network.
