TI  - Layered image data real-time drawing method for            three-dimensional terrain, involves reading slice of            each hierarchy of current view port area, sequentially            mixing all levels of slices, outputting image, and            drawing image on terrain grid
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The layered image data real-time drawing                method involves storing a tile set of an area                terrain in a server. A first network address is                issued. An image service catalog each layer image                is stored into the server. The second network                address of the current view port area is obtained.                The level of the map service catalog is read. An                index address is constructed by using information                in the picture service catalog. A slice of each                hierarchy of a current view port area is read                according to the index address. The image is                sequentially mixed with all levels of slices to                output the image and draw the image on the terrain                grid.
                    USE - Layered image data real-time drawing method                for three-dimensional terrain visualization                technology used in military, agriculture, traffic,                smart city and other industries.
                    ADVANTAGE - The layered image data real-time drawing                method using interpolation method for fusing the                image data of different layer level, the layer                breaking and pasteurizing is eliminated, and the                image blurring or pasteurization is prevented. The                security and transmission of the data of high                efficiency is ensured. The accuracy of the access                path is ensured, the call of the mass slice data is                not error, the server and the virtual engine can be                fast and high efficient data connection, and                satisfy amount is larger.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a layered                image data real-time drawing system has a tile                storage module for storing the tile set of the area                terrain in the server.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow chart of a layered                image data real-time drawing method. (Drawing                includes non-English language text).
