TI  - Multi-path component clustering and tracking            method for unmanned aerial vehicle channel estimation            used in e.g. military communication field, involves            performing dynamic adjustment to obtain multiple            clusters at current time according to boundary            threshold and density threshold pair cluster
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves obtaining the unmanned                aerial vehicle channel data at the initial time.                The multi-path components at the previous time and                the current time are optimally matched according to                the characteristic parameters. The multi-path                component matched at the current time and the                multi-path component not matched at the current                time are obtained. The multi-path component matched                with the current time is directly distributed to                the cluster corresponding to the multi-path                component matched with the current time. The                multi-path component which is not matched at the                current time is distributed to the corresponding                cluster by using the classification model middle,                to obtain cluster. The boundary threshold and                density threshold are calculated according to the                cluster. The dynamic adjustment is performed to                obtain multiple clusters at the current time                according to boundary threshold and density                threshold pair cluster.
                    USE - Multi-path component clustering and tracking                method for unmanned aerial vehicle channel                estimation used in fields of military                communication, disaster rescue, logistics                transportation and smart city.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method dynamically optimizes by                introducing boundary threshold value, density                threshold value and classification model, which                obviously improves the precision of channel                clustering and enhances the adaptive capacity of                time-varying channel.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram illustrating                the multi-path component clustering and tracking                method for unmanned aerial vehicle channel                estimation. (Drawing includes non-English language                text)
