TI  - Method for assigning time-slot and            channel-frequency-hopping schedule to e.g. sensor            access points for military applications, involves            assigning frequency offsets to network devices based on            communication schedule
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method (1000) involves identifying                neighboring devices for each network device (1015)                based on locations of the network devices along an                intelligent wire. A communication schedule is                determined for the network devices (1020) to                prevent neighboring devices along the intelligent                wire from transmitting data with same frequency.                The network devices are assigned to communication                time slots (1025) based on the communication                schedule. Frequency offsets are assigned to the                network devices (1030) based on the communication                schedule.
                    USE - Method for assigning a communication schedule                i.e. time-slot and channel-frequency-hopping                schedule, to low power and lossy network devices                e.g. sensor access points, Wi-Fi access points and                LED access points (all claimed), along an                intelligent wire for a low power and lossy network                i.e. smart object or sensor networks, for                industrial smart grid and military applications and                smart cities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables providing a packet                scheduling mechanism that utilizes physical                locations of network devices along the intelligent                wire to generate the communication schedule, thus                minimizing interference between neighboring devices                along the wire and simplifying maintenance of                intelligent wire as the sensors do not need to be                replaced when faulty due to high density. The                method enables reducing emission power used in the                intelligent wire for minimizing power consumed by                the intelligent wire.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for an                apparatus for assigning a communication schedule to                network devices along an intelligent wire.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow chart illustrating a                procedure for assigning a communication schedule to                network devices along an intelligent wire.1000Method for assigning communication                schedule to network devices along intelligent                wire1015Step for identifying neighboring devices                for each network device1020Step for determining communication                schedule for network devices1025Step for assigning network devices to                communication time slots1030Step for assigning frequency offsets to                network devices
