TI  - Method for detecting image target based on            multiple receptive fields pyramid involves inputting            extracted candidate area to cascade area convolution            neural network training, and performing target            detection to image to be detected
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves constructing a ResNet-50                feature extraction network and a cascade region                convolutional neural network to obtain an image                training set. The image training sets are used as                the input of the ResNet 50 feature extract network                to extract the image features of the image training                group. The extraction network is extracted                according to a preset multiple receptive fields                pyramid and a preset interest area. The candidate                area of the extracted image features is extracted.                The extracted candidate area is inputted to the                cascade area convolution neural network training.                The neural network is trained after the training is                completed. The target detection is performed on the                image to be detected to obtain a detection                result.
                    USE - Image target detection method for use in                military reconnaissance, smart city management and                accurate agriculture or industry. Can also be used                in image target detection device based on                characteristic pyramid of multiple receptive                fields.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables avoiding lack of                considering a receptive field in an existing                technology, thus increasing semantic information of                the receptive field, combining characteristic                pyramid and receptive field two angles, and                improving multi-scale target detection performance.                The method allows a training detection module to                perform image feature extraction on the image                training set by constructing ResNet-50 feature                extraction network and cascade region convolution                neural network and extracting network according to                the preset multiple receptive fields pyramid and                the preset interest region, thus extracting the                candidate area of the image feature, and hence                avoiding the lack of the feeling field in the                existing technology.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for an                image target detection device based on                characteristic pyramid of multiple receptive                fields.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flowchart illustrating                the method for detecting image target based on                multiple receptive fields pyramid (Drawing includes                non-English language text).
