TI  - Fitting goodness test based global satellite            navigation system spoofing attack detection method,            involves judging whether current GNSS receiver is in            deception attack stage according to correlator test            statistic
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves counting distribution                characteristics related to a related integral                amplitude value after a non-deception attack stage                P-correlator. A corresponding theoretical                distribution parameter is obtained. A GNSS receiver                tracking stage P-correlator, an E-correlator and an                output value of an L-correlator are obtained. The                output value is detected by using a Chi2GoF test. A                P-collator test statistic is constructed according                to the relevant output amplitude change and the                theoretical distribution parameters after the                P-colonist. A difference between output values of                the E-collators and the L-collaborators is detected                through a double-sample testing method.                Determination is made to check whether the current                GNSS receivers are in a deception attack                stage.
                    USE - Fitting goodness test based global satellite                navigation system (GNSS) spoofing attack detection                method for national economy e.g. power grid                monitoring, financial system, communication system,                smart city, precision agriculture and national                defense security e.g. military astronautics and                accurate guidance weapons.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables effectively combining                complementary characteristics two test methods in                different power advantage spoofing attack detection                effect, and exerts the high sensitivity advantage                of fitting goodness test to sample data change,                under the fraud attack of detecting various power                advantages. The method enables showing high                sensitivity and robustness, and effectively and                reliably deceiving attack detection scheme.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic flow diagram of                a fitting goodness test based GNSS spoofing attack                detection method (Drawing includes non-English                language text).
