TI  - System for detecting malicious nodes in wireless            sensor network used in environmental monitoring and            military surveillance, comprises ranking unit that is            designed to rank node metrics and network metrics based            on statistical significance in identifying malicious            nodes
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) comprises a set of sensor                nodes (104) that are deployed in wireless sensor                network (WSN) (102). A data acquisition unit (108)                is connected to the sensor nodes operably designed                to monitor a set of nodes in wireless sensor                network to obtain node metrics comprising packet                rate, packet drop rate, packet duplication rate,                signal strength, signal-to-noise ratio, error rate,                central processing unit (CPU) usage, memory usage,                and bandwidth usage for each of set of nodes. The                wireless sensor network is monitored to obtain                network metrics comprising data throughput, energy                consumption rate, number of neighbors, route                request frequency, route reply frequency, data                transmission frequency, and data reception                frequency. A ranking unit (110) is operably                configured to rank node metrics and network metrics                based on their statistical significance in                identifying malicious nodes. A cluster head (CH)                (112) is coupled with data acquisition unit and                ranking unit.
                    USE - System for detecting malicious nodes in                wireless sensor network (WSN) used in environmental                monitoring and military surveillance to smart                cities and industrial automation.
                    ADVANTAGE - The dual-stage system for malicious node                detection in wireless sensor networks (WSNs),                effectively integrating hybrid machine learning                (ML) techniques to enhance security is provided.                The adaptive dynamic threshold detection mechanism                at the cluster head (CH) level that dynamically                adjusts detection parameters based on both current                CH resource availability and feature                characteristics, optimizing resource utilization                and maintaining detection performance is                implemented. The real-time MN detection capability                that allows for timely responses to security                threats is provided and minimizes potential damage                from malicious activities within the WSN. The                mechanisms i.e. decentralized, verifiable, and                tamper-proof mechanism significantly enhance the                system's resilience and scalability, enabling                secure, efficient, and accurate malicious node                detection even in large-scale and heterogeneous WSN                deployments.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                for detecting malicious nodes in a wireless sensor                network.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a system                for detecting malicious nodes in a wireless sensor                network.100Wireless sensor network malicious nodes                detecting system102Wireless sensor network104sensor nodes108data acquisition unit110Ranking unit112cluster head
