TI  - Dynamically adaptive kinetic self-healing wireless            mesh network system used in internet of things (IoT)            ecosystem, has nodes, each of which is equipped with            adaptive routing modules for continuous topology            optimization
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The dynamically adaptive kinetic self-healing                wireless mesh network system has several                interconnected nodes (1), each of which is equipped                with adaptive routing modules (2) for continuous                topology optimization. A kinetic self-healing                control unit autonomously detects and repairs node                or link failures by rerouting traffic. A predictive                analytics within the control unit forecast the                potential failures to enable preemptive topology                reconfiguration. An energy-aware optimization                module (4) balances workload across nodes to                conserve energy and extend lifespan. A modular                architecture interface enables scalability and                interoperability across heterogeneous                environments.
                    USE - Dynamically adaptive kinetic self-healing                wireless mesh network system. Uses include but are                not limited to disaster recovery, military                communication, rural connectivity, smart city                infrastructure, and internet of things (IoT)                ecosystem.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system restores the connectivity under                node failures, mobility, or environmental                disruptions. The system ensures uninterrupted                communication, reduced downtime, and optimized                resource utilization across heterogeneous wireless                infrastructures, by integrating kinetic self-repair                mechanisms with adaptive routing protocols. The                network ensures uninterrupted connectivity under                varying conditions. The energy-efficient routing                mechanism minimizes the resource wastage during                topology reconfigurations. The system provides                continuous wireless connectivity through dynamic                self-healing, reducing service disruptions in                mission-critical applications. The system provides                proactive fault detection and predictive healing,                and minimizes the downtime and latency. The system                provides the energy-efficient routing, thus                extending the operational lifespan of network                nodes. The system provides scalability, allowing                seamless deployment in both small-scale and                large-scale environments. The system provides the                modular design and interoperability, thus enabling                the integration with existing communication                infrastructures.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of the dynamically adaptive kinetic self-healing                wireless mesh network.1Interconnected node2Adaptive routing module4Energy-aware optimization module
