TI  - System for verifying location information of            unmanned mobile vehicle e.g. drones and preventing            attacks such as global positioning system spoofing, has            unmanned mobile device that generates data structure,            and verifies location information of access points            using generated data structure
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has multiple access points                (102-1-102-5). A data storage unit (104) stores and                manages identification information (ID) and                location information of each of multiple access                points. An unmanned mobile device (106) receives                the identification information and the location                information of multiple access points corresponding                to its movement path (108) from the data storage                unit, generates a data structure, and verifies                location information of access points using the                generated data structure. The data storage unit                stores and manages the identification information                and the location information using a blockchain                network.
                    USE - System for verifying location information of                unmanned mobile vehicle e.g. drones (claimed) and                preventing attacks such as global positioning                system (GPS) spoofing of unmanned mobile vehicle                used in various fields including personal hobbies,                agriculture, logistics, fire and rescue, traffic                surveillance, and military weapons.
                    ADVANTAGE - The hacking attacks such as GPS spoofing                attacks of unmanned vehicles are effectively                blocked by verifying the location information of                unmanned vehicles using smart city infrastructure                such as access points located near the route the                unmanned vehicle intends to travel. The only                information about access points located on the                movement path of the unmanned mobile vehicle is                selectively stored in the unmanned mobile vehicle,                rather than information about the access points of                the entire city, and the storage space of the                unmanned vehicle is utilized efficiently, thus the                time to search for the access point closest to the                current location of the unmanned vehicle is                shortened. The resource usage of unmanned mobile                devices required for authentication is effectively                reduced compared to the case of connecting to                multiple access points each time authentication by                performing secondary authentication using multiple                access points only when wireless connection is not                possible.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:an unmanned mobile vehicle; anda method for verifying location                information.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic diagram                illustrating the system for verifying location                information.100System for verifying location                information102-1-102-5Access points104Data storage unit106Unmanned mobile device108Movement path
