TI  - Hybrid deep neural network-based intrusion            detection system for e.g. smart applications, has            classification module associated with feature            extraction module, where fully connected layer            determines class details of input image
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (100) has a dataset creation module                (102) for creating a dataset with real-world input                data, where the dataset contains data regarding                interaction with intrusion detection (ID) traffic                input and a label element indicating connection                state as normal or attacked. A data pre-processing                module (104) is associated with the dataset                creation module to formulate the input data based                on a set of pre-processing submodules. A feature                extraction module (106) is connected to the data                pre-processing module for extracting a set of                feature maps, where the feature extraction module                comprises a set of convolution layers to perform a                convolution function on the feature maps and                transfer to a next layer. A classification module                (108) is associated with the feature extraction                module, and includes a dropout layer and                densely-connected classifier, where a fully                connected layer (FCL) determines class details of                the input image based on visual information                extracted by the convolution layers.
                    USE - Hybrid deep neural network-based ID system for                smart applications. Uses include but are not                limited to smart healthcare applications, smart                city applications, military applications, aerospace                applications, and environmental monitoring                applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system learns characteristics of data                through a convolution neural network (CNN) phase,                and drives into a long short-term memory (LSTM)                phase which deliberates past and future information                about the input data, thus facilitating optimal                utilizing of blocks and maintaining time-series                information in a combination of CNN and LSTM model                and obtaining accurate classification of various                modern attacks.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a hybrid                deep neural network-based ID system.100Hybrid deep neural network-based ID                system102Dataset creation module104Data pre-processing module106Feature extraction module108Classification module
