TI  - Method for proactively adjusting broadcast            capacity used for quick joins of smart objects,            involves instructing nodes to use normal schedule in            response to determining that degree of network            functionality exceeds amount
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves instructing nodes (200) in                a network (100) to use a network formation                broadcast schedule during an upcoming network                formation event. A determination is made that                degree of functionality in the network during the                event exceeds threshold amount. The nodes are                instructed to use a normal broadcast schedule in                response to determining that the degree of                functionality in the network during the event                exceeds the threshold amount, where channels of the                network formation broadcast schedule are active                more frequently than channels of the normal                broadcast schedule when in use.
                    USE - Method for proactively adjusting broadcast                capacity used for quick joins of smart objects over                a computer network e.g. low power and lossy network                (LLN) such as sensor network e.g. smart object                network or shared-media network such as wireless or                power line communication network. Uses include but                are not limited to interconnect light devices,                appliances, vehicles, heating, ventilating and                air-conditioning devices, windows, window shades                and blinds, doors, locks and sensors, for smart                grids, smart cities, building and industrial                automation applications, cars and military                applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables providing a message with                prefix information to identify destinations,                capability to record routes in support of source                routing, and information to determine freshness of                particular advertisement. The method enables                increasing broadcast capacity in a decentralized                channel-hopping network for quicker network                formation as neighbor discovery occurs efficiently                and removing channel-hopping dimension from a                discovery protocol, while reducing spectral                diversity.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for an                apparatus for proactively adjusting broadcast                capacity used for quick network joins for computer                networks.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of a communication network.100Network105Links130Wide area network140Data packets150Servers200Nodes in network
