TI  - Miniaturized satellite system for weather            monitoring and location tracking using long range            project, has global positioning system module that is            configured to collect atmospheric and location data and            transmit data through long range communication to            ground station
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has an embedded controller (ESP32),                environmental sensors including temperature,                humidity and pressure sensors, and a global                positioning system module, configured to collect                atmospheric and location data and transmit data                through long range (LoRa) communication to a ground                station. The LoRa communication module enables                long-range, low-power transmission exceeding 3                kilometers, independent of cellular or internet                infrastructure, and is suitable for deployment in                remote or disaster-prone areas.
                    USE - Miniaturized satellite system for weather                monitoring and location tracking using LoRa                project, and applied to disaster management and                early warning systems, agricultural planning,                environmental research and climate studies, and                military and defense surveillance used for                environmental awareness, internet of things and                smart city integration, and educational and                training purposes in schools, colleges, and                universities to teach students about satellites,                wire wireless communication, and environmental                sensing.
                    ADVANTAGE - The low cost mini satellites and LoRa modules                are much cheaper than traditional satellite                systems, and made ideal for academic, research, or                small-scale projects. The long-range communication                transmits data over several kilometers, even in                remote areas, without needing cellular networks or                internet access. The system uses very little power,                and allows for long-term deployment with small                batteries or solar panels. The system provides live                temperature, humidity, and pressure data, useful                for local weather forecasting and analysis. The                accurate location tracking GPS integration allows                real-time tracking of the satellite's position,                which is essential for navigation and environmental                studies. The compact size of the mini satellite                makes it easy to launch using weather balloons or                drones, without the need for heavy equipment. The                scalability multiple satellites or sensor nodes are                deployed to cover larger areas or collect more                detailed data. The system does not depend on mobile                towers or internet, and is made ideal for rural,                mountainous, or disaster-hit areas. The system                supports disaster management and used to monitor                weather changes and track locations during natural                disasters such as floods or storms, helping in                early warning and rescue operations.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                for autonomous environmental monitoring.
