TI  - Method for facilitating traffic class capacity            allocation in low power and lossy sensor networks for            e.g. military applications, involves providing channel            assignment that assigns particular traffic class to            particular channel to nodes
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves identifying traffic                classes used by nodes (11-13, 21-24, 31-34, 41-45)                in a computer network (100). Routing requirements                for a particular traffic class of the traffic                classes is determined by a communicating device                (200). A channel assignment that assigns the                particular traffic class to a particular channel is                generated based on the routing requirements for the                particular traffic class by the device. The channel                assignment is provided to the nodes, where the                nodes use the channel assignment to route traffic                of the particular traffic class within the                network.
                    USE - Method for facilitating traffic class capacity                allocation in computer networks or low power and                lossy sensor networks. Uses include but are not                limited to time division multiple access (TDMA),                frequency division multiple access networks,                shared-media networks i.e. wireless or power line                communication networks, field area networks,                neighborhood area networks and personal area                networks for smart grids, smart cities, building                and industrial automation applications and military                applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables designing a distributed                mesh architecture of the network to minimize                increase in communication delay by combining fast                re-route techniques for the networks, in a                distributed mesh network structure. The method                enables realizing flexibility of                carrier-sense-multiple-access with effective                capacity allocation of the networks, while                combining channel allocations to traffic classes                with fast re-route mechanisms in a full mesh                environment.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included for the                following:an apparatus for facilitating traffic class                capacity allocation in computer networksa tangible non-transitory computer-readable                medium comprising a set of instructions for                facilitating traffic class capacity allocation in                computer networks.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of a communication network.11-13, 21-24, 31-34, 41-45Nodes100Computer network140Data packets150Management devices/servers200Communicating device
