TI  - Lossless compression method for grid tile integer            data based on distance information, involves inserting            pyramid inside information compressed data, and quickly            decompressing to obtain all original data of grid tile            data
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves setting the data distance                threshold according to the power of 2 for the                original raster tile data under any layer and row,                according to the maximum number of bits occupied by                a single data value. The case is expanded where the                distance is 0 and exceeds the distance that is                represented by the maximum number of bits, and                calculate the threshold range. All the compressed                data of the original raster tile data are assembled                to form the lossless compressed data of the                original raster tile data under this layer and row.                The maximum number of bits of the original raster                tile data is used to save the minimum value of the                raster data in the front of the compressed data All                the original data of the raster tile data is                quickly decompressed without additionally                generating an index file through the embedded                pyramid index information of the compressed data                such as layer number, row number and column number                of the compressed data.
                    USE - Lossless compression method for grid tile                integer data based on distance information for                civil and military fields. Uses include but are not                limited to smart city, surveying and mapping                engineering, urban planning and military                application of commanding decision-making and task                planning.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method reduces the storage consumption by                reducing the binary bit consumption of the grid                integer data base, through the minimum value,                proper compressed bit position, and minimum value                of the distance to information the whole                information the grid tile whole type data, thus                realizing the fast decompression recovery of the                needed grid tile data, improving the convenience of                the data use, and reducing the data in                transportation, maintenance and storage.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram illustrating                the lossless compression method for grid tile                integer data based on distance information.                (Drawing includes non-English language text)
