TI  - Hybrid sustainable power generation (HSPG) system            for rooftop or confined urban installation, has shared            transmission line and direct current (DC) bus bar that            is used for distributing energy from both solar and            wind subsystems
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a solar photovoltaic (PV) array                configured in a series-parallel arrangement and                mounted on a tilt-adjustable structure. The array                includes monocrystalline or polycrystalline solar                panels. A wind turbine is selected from either a                horizontal axis wind turbine (HAWT) or a vertical                axis wind turbine (VAWT). A hybrid power control                system comprises a maximum power point tracking                (MPPT) controller, a rectifier for converting                alternating current (AC) output from the wind                turbine into DC, and a hybrid charge controller                configured to manage combined energy input from                both solar and wind sources. An energy storage                system comprises a battery bank and a DC-to-AC                inverter for providing pure sine wave AC output. A                microcontroller-based energy management system                (EMS) is configured to monitor real-time                environmental and system parameters and to control                energy distribution, and a shared transmission line                and DC bus bar is used for distributing energy from                both solar and wind subsystems.
                    USE - Hybrid sustainable power generation (HSPG)                system for rooftop or confined urban installation                on commercial building such as office building,                mall, hotel and data center, deployed to power                smart lighting and surveillance system such as                Wireless fidelity (Wi-Fi)hotspot, closed-circuit TV                (CCTV) cameras, and ambient lighting in                residential, commercial and industrial                applications. Can also be used in smart city and                urban infrastructure, telecommunications sector,                agricultural and agro-processing industry,                industrial manufacturing plant and defense and                military operations at high-altitude location,                mounted on ship, or integrated into mobile command                unit in battlefield scenarios and deployed to power                communication device, medical equipment, and water                purification system in temporary shelter or field                hospital.
                    ADVANTAGE - The HSPG system can maximize energy production                through the simultaneous use of both solar and wind                energy, enable efficient distribution of power                generated by solar panels and windmills to specific                destinations as required, and can facilitate easy                installation in a variety of settings such as                residential, commercial and industrial                applications. The HSPG system can ensure higher                overall energy production and increased system                efficiency when compared to standalone solar and                wind systems, can promote sustainable power                generation by reducing reliance on traditional                fossil fuels and minimizing carbon emissions, and                can support the transition towards an                eco-friendlier and sustainable energy future.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows the schematic diagram of                the HSPG system.
