TI  - Unified peripheral hardware interaction interface            for internet of things (IOT) terminal, has peripheral            output coding unit that is utilized for performing data            encapsulation on peripheral output according to            specified data encapsulation format
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The interface has a pin configuration unit                that is used for configuring the connection mode                and the electrical characteristics of each pin for                the inserted peripheral under the remote control                instruction sent by the gateway. The connection                mode comprises a connection mode of a control                signal and a connection mode of a data signal. The                input signal generating unit is used for analyzing                the control instruction sent by the gateway and                generating a specific physical signal required by                accessing a target peripheral according to the data                communication protocol core configured by the pin                configuration unit. The peripheral output coding                unit is used for performing data encapsulation on                peripheral output according to a specified data                encapsulation format and uploading the peripheral                output to the gateway based on the data                communication protocol core configured by the pin                configuration unit. The peripheral output includes                a data output and a status output.
                    USE - Unified peripheral hardware interaction                interface for internet of things (IOT) terminal                used in fields such as industry, smart city, smart                medical treatment and military disputes.
                    ADVANTAGE - The interaction interface greatly improves the                compatibility of the IOT terminal to different                peripherals, avoids the program update of the                Internet of things terminal and reduces the                technical cost of customized development of the IOT                terminal by controlling the communication between                the terminal and the peripherals by generating the                control instruction by the gateway. The user does                not need to rewrite and burn programs of the                terminal and controls the new peripheral by only                modifying the control instruction sent by the                gateway when a new peripheral is replaced. The                device capable of sending binary data streams with                specific formats can realize control on different                peripheral equipment through the unified peripheral                equipment interaction interface. The compatibility                of the IOT terminal with different peripherals is                obviously improved.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic structural                diagram of a pin configuration unit of a unified                peripheral interaction interface. (Drawing includes                non-English language text)
