TI  - Artificial intelligence-powered automated video            surveillance and threat detection device for use in            e.g. public safety applications, has edge processing            module for performing real-time analytics locally to            reduce latency and bandwidth consumption
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The device has an edge processing module (120)                for performing real-time analytics locally to                reduce latency and bandwidth consumption. An                artificial intelligence (AI) analytics module (130)                incorporates deep learning algorithms for facial                recognition, behavior analysis, and object                detection. A threat detection engine (140)                categorizes detected anomalies into multi-level                severity classes for context based alerts. A                communication interface ensures secure data                transmission using encrypted protocols for threat                alerts. A power management unit (180) integrates                renewable energy or battery backup for                uninterrupted functioning.
                    USE - AI-powered automated video surveillance and                threat detection device for use in public safety,                industrial security and asset protection                applications for integrating advanced computer                vision, deep learning models, and edge-based                analytics to identify, classify, and alert                potential security threats in real-time, reducing                human dependency while improving accuracy,                scalability, and proactive security management                across diverse environments. Uses include but are                not limited to smart cities, airports, banks,                military zones and corporate facilities.
                    ADVANTAGE - The device is scalable, real-time, accurate,                and capable of functioning in both indoor and                outdoor environments under varied lighting and                weather conditions. The system prioritizes data                security and privacy, ensuring that sensitive                information is protected from unauthorized access.                The device provides a self-learning mechanism where                AI models continuously adapt to new environments,                enhancing detection accuracy over time. The                edge-enabled device is capable of processing video                streams locally, thus reducing latency and                bandwidth consumption. The multi-modal integration                is provided by combining video, audio, and motion                sensors to improve situational awareness. The                seamless integration with security infrastructure                such as alarms, access control, and emergency                communication systems is provided, enabling                automated incident response. The device                autonomously detects suspicious activities,                classifies threat severity, and issues real-time                alerts to relevant stakeholders, realizes that the                hybrid architecture combines edge-based processing                for low latency with cloud integration for                continuous learning and large-scale data                management, is designed with energy efficiency and                secure communication protocols. The device reduces                human dependency, enhances situational awareness,                and ensures proactive, scalable, and reliable                surveillance across multiple environments.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of an                AI-powered automated video surveillance and threat                detection device.110Camera units120Edge processing module130AI analytics module140Threat detection engine180Power management unit
