TI  - Method for estimating position of e.g. smartphone,            in environment in different applications, involves            calculating position of device at required time based            on ranges and/or angles and adjusted anchor positions,            and adjusting position of anchor involved in            observation by displacement
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves receiving first set of                observations (30) taken at different times between                a device (20) and a distributed anchor (15), where                the observations are taken by first set of sensors                (22). A time window is defined for a required time                for the position of the device to be estimated for                the observation taken at a time point in a time                window. A range and/or angle are estimated from the                device to the anchor from the observation                estimating the displacement of the device due to                motion between the time the observation to be taken                and the required time, where the displacement is                estimated based on observations taken by second set                of sensors. A position of the anchor involved in                the observation by the displacement is adjusted to                compensate for effect of the motion of the device.                A position of the device is calculated at the                required time based on the ranges and/or angles and                the adjusted anchor positions.
                    USE - Method for estimating a position of a mobile                device (claimed) such as smartphone, tablet and                mobile computing device, or object in an                environment in different applications. Uses include                but are not limited to smart cities, Internet of                Things (loT), medical services, automotive                industry, underwater exploration, public safety,                and military systems.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables improving location                accuracy. The method enables improving positioning                techniques and mitigate or avoid schemes noted                above by providing a positioning scheme so as to                realize simple to set up, accurate, and robust even                in challenging environments. The method enables                providing fusing range and displacement                measurements within a time window to estimate a                position of a moving object at a required time. The                method enables allowing the position of the device                to be estimated relative to the anchors. The method                enables effectively determining hidden state and                producing highly accurate positions by using                sizable number of Bluetooth (RTM: Wireless data                communications protocol) observations.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for:(1) a method for estimating a hidden state                variables associated with dynamics of a C\J device                moving in an environment;(2) a computer program comprising a set of                instructions for estimating a position of a mobile                device or object in an environment;(3) a system for estimating a position of a                mobile device or object in an environment.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of a positioning system for estimating a position                of a mobile device in an environment.15Distributed anchor20Device22Sensors26Processing Unit30Observations
