TI  - Method for iteratively controlling movement of            agents e.g. robot by processors, involves receiving            target signal indicating location of target from first            sensor associated with agent, and updating probability            map by agent based on received target signal
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves receiving (S1005) an                initial probability map, comprising probability                values, each representing probability of location                of targets in an area of interest by agent, and                applying (S1010) a neural network (NN) model on the                probability map to produce based on the probability                values, predicted cumulative reward (PCR) values,                where PCR values correspond to respective optional                movement actions of the agent, and predict a future                cumulative reward representing aggregation of data                in the probability map by the agents. A movement                action of the optional movement actions are                selected (S1015) based on the PCR values. The agent                is moved (S1020) according to the selected movement                action. A target signal indicating a location of                target of the targets are received (S1025) from                first sensor associated with the agent. The                probability map is updated (S1030) by agent based                on the received target signal.
                    USE - Method for iteratively controlling movement of                agents such as drones and robots, by processors.                Uses include but are not limited to military                applications, homeland security applications such                as border protection, protection of facilities such                as pipelines, airports, industrial areas, maritime                domain awareness, and civilian applications that                rely on probability maps for smart city maintenance                such as searching for water or sewage leakage,                searching for electric grid failures, and providing                location-based services such as distribution of                elements such as goods, food, drink and                medication.
                    ADVANTAGE - The simulation verifies the training method                and demonstrate a decrease in the temporal                difference learning error with an increasing number                of learning epochs.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:a system for iteratively controlling agent;                anda method of distributed controlling of                movement of agents.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram illustrating                a method for controlling agents based on a                reinforcement learning, or Q- leaming                algorithm.S1005Step for receiving an initial                probability map, comprising probability values,                each representing probability of location of                targets in an area of interest by agentS1010Step for applying a NN model on the                probability map to produce based on the probability                values, PCR valuesS1015Step for selecting a movement action of                the optional movement actions based on the PCR                valuesS1020Step for moving the agent according to                the selected movement actionS1025Step for receiving a target signal                indicating a location of target of the targets from                first sensor associated with the agentS1030Step for updating the probability map by                the agent based on the received target                signal
