TI  - Method for audio processing of unmanned aerial            vehicle (UAV) such as drones used for aerial surveys,            mapping, involves determining whether separate target            audio source signal is associated with target audio            sources, and inputting separate signal into classifying            neural network
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method (600) involves receiving a mixed                audio signal with a set of audio sources by a                processor circuitry (602). The mixed signal is                separated into a separate target audio source                signal (620). A determination is made whether the                separate target signal is associated with the                target source by inputting the separate signal into                a classifying neural network (624). The target                source is selected from one of a moving object that                emits sound, a transport, a vehicle, a drone, an                unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV), a helicopter, and an                animal. Source audio signals of different drones                are separated. Mixed audio signal data of the mixed                signal are input into an audio signature                mask-estimate-based neural network.
                    USE - Method for audio processing of UAV such as                drones used for aerial surveys, mapping, geographic                information system (GIS) data collection,                infrastructure inspection, construction, smart-city                applications, package delivery, and military                uses.
