TI  - System for supporting urban scanning in fixed            hotspot access network, has mobile access point for            communicating obtained sensory information and/or            information relating to obtained sensory information            through fixed access point
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has communication circuits for                communication of signals for transmission and                reception of data. A mobile access point (MAP)                obtains sensory information during operations in an                infrastructure utilized by the MAPs, stores the                sensory information within the MAP, and determines                when access to a central entity in a communication                network is available through a fixed access point                (FAP) (703-1). A central entity manages                infrastructure and/or the communication network.                The MAP communicates the obtained sensory                information and/or information relating to the                obtained sensory information through the FAP.
                    USE - System for supporting urban scanning in a                communication network i.e. fixed hotspot access                network, using self-organized fleets of AV. Can                also be used for a in-vehicle network,                maritime/watercraft network, port network, general                controlled-space network, residential network,                disaster recovery and emergency network, military                and aircraft network, smart city network,                event/venue network, underwater/underground                network, agricultural network,                tunnel/auto/Underground Railway/train network,                parking network, security and surveillance network,                shipping equipment and container network,                environmental control or monitoring network,                municipal network, waste management network, road                maintenance network, traffic management network,                and advertising network.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system can be flexibly optimized at                design/installation time and/or in real-time for                different purposes to reduce the latency, increase                throughput, reduce power consumption, load balance,                increase reliability and make more robust with                regard to failures or other disturbances based on                content, service or data that the platform provides                or handles within a particular environment. The                system enables actors to join forces and act                together to build and manage a scalable,                high-performance, robust and safe ecosystem in                which autonomous vehicles (AVs) are the central                point to provide high-value services so as to                optimize network capacity, reduce congestion on                roads, make a passenger's journey stress free,                positively impact community and socio-economic                growth, increase safety and improve fleet                operations. The system provides smart                transportation that coordinates operations and                rides to reduce number of vehicles and avoid                congestion on the roads and competition for parking                spaces, thus providing for high-quality and highly                efficient transportation and improved user                mobility. The system leverages the connectivity                among AVs, thus enabling AVs to immediately share                knowledge with one another and with cloud, thus                increasing overall safety of autonomous driving and                navigation on the roads and highways.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                method for performing urban scanning in a                communication network.
