TI  - Hacking defense system for protecting personal            information based on structure, has immutable log            recording module that structures detection events in            JavaScript Object Notation format and records them in            blockchain or distributed storage after hashing and            electronic signature
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a unit cube (110) for each unit                time (TSU) defined based on an absolute starting                point. An intra-block verification module (200)                verifies phase correlation within a unit cube. An                inter-block verification module (210) performs                anchor-to-anchor cross-validation between adjacent                Q-Blocks (120). A restoration and isolation module                (300) performs automatic restoration by referring                to previous TSU and adjacent unit cubes when an                anomaly is detected, and isolates entire unit cube                or Q-Block in case of repeated restoration                failures. An anchor policy gate module (400)                enforces tokenization, de-identification, and                masking in unavoidable cases. An immutable log                recording module (500) structures detection events                in format and records them in a blockchain or                distributed storage (600) after hashing and                electronic signature. A policy optimization module                (700) receives system events as input and performs                reinforcement learning-based policy updates.
                    USE - Hacking defense system for protecting personal                information in Q-Block structure based on structure                used in industry such as finance, healthcare,                public sector, and metaverse. Can also be used in                hospital and medical system, transportation and                smart city infrastructure, and military and defense                system.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system integrates a layered structure                based on a unit cube and a Q-Block and an anchor                policy gate module at the architectural level, thus                preventing the existence of sensitive information                plaintext within the system, and forcing a                tokenization/de-identification path even when                storage is unavoidable. The unit cube stacking is                simply based on relative event order or local                timestamp, which increases the possibility of false                positives or false negatives due to network delays                or time differences during the inter-block                verification process, makes the system vulnerable                to delay and reuse attacks, and reduces restoration                reliability.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for the                following:a hacking prevention method for protecting                personal information in Q-Block structure for                protecting personal information in Q-Block                structure; anda computer-readable recording medium storing                program for protecting personal information in                Q-Block structure.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic view of a                hacking defense system.110Unit cube120Q-block200Intra-block verification module210Inter-block verification module300Restoration and isolation module400Anchor policy gate module500Immutable log recording module600Blockchain or distributed storage700Policy optimization module
