TI  - System for providing live video windows to client            end e.g. game console from airborne platform i.e.            unmanned aerial vehicle for military applications, has            server system for receiving live video requests from            client end and delivering live video feed of region of            interest of scene to client end
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a composite focal plane array                (CFPA) imaging system (300) installed on an                airborne platform. A CFPA camera (310) is provided                with focal plane array (FPA) sensor modules. An                image processing subsystem (301) is provided with                nodes in communication with a global client node by                interconnects (340). The node is programmed to                process image data from the CFPA camera according                to video window corresponding to a scene area of                interest. A server system receives live video                requests from a client end over a network and                delivers live video feed of a region of the                interest of the scene to the client end over the                network.
                    USE - System for simultaneously providing live video                windows to a client end i.e. unmanned aerial                vehicle (claimed) from an airborne platform. Uses                include but are not limited to mobile telephone, a                personal digital assistant (PDA), a mobile audio or                video player, a game console, a global positioning                system(GPS) receiver, or a portable storage device                i.e. universal serial bus(USB) flash(RTM: Computer                multimedia application) drive for public safety,                insurance, disaster relief, search and rescue,                smart cities, border surveillance and military                applications.
                    ADVANTAGE - The system realizes onboard parallel                processing of image data for fulfilling                simultaneous live video window requests to reduce                bandwidth demands on wireless data link required to                fulfill the requests, mechanically maintains an                arrangement of elements of the camera and protects                the camera from environmental sources of damage or                interference and compresses a mosaic image in                lossless format to allow original data                reconstructed from compressed data with reduced                loss of information. The system reduces data size                of the mosaic image which reduces transfer data                rate between components of the CFPA video system,                storage space in a storage device, and time to                perform image resampling process for video stream                creation. The system restricts processing to the                region of the interest portions to reduce                computational cost and time to complete resampling                and production of the video streams.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                for simultaneously providing live video windows to                a client end from an airborne platform.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of an CFPA                imaging system.300CFPA imaging system301Image processing subsystem310CFPA camera320Global processing node340,342Interconnects
