TI  - Conversation augmentation system for use as            virtual assistant for enabling artificial intelligence            assisted conversation between vehicles and operators            using biosensor, has computing device for using user            experience engine to present conversation feature to            user and accept input data from user
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system has a biosensor for receiving                biosignals. A perception engine receives sensory                input e.g. audio data, and parsing the biosignals.                The perception engine consumes multimodal sensory                information from one of cameras, microphones, and                other data streams of sensory inputs, where                perception engine output is stored by a memory                engine (500). A conversation engine (300) consumes                content and instructions to orchestrate prompts                that produce data to be communicated when the                content and instructions are sent to a conversation                language model (LM) (310). A refinement engine                allows the user to approve and modify responses                before generating a conversation output (124). A                computing device uses a user experience engine                (200) to present a conversation feature (120) to a                user and accept input data from the user. A                companion application generates communications to a                conversation partner, which is one of a human                partner and a machine agent.
                    USE - Conversation augmentation system for use as a                virtual assistant for enabling an AI assisted                conversation between humans e.g. individuals with                disabilities, surgeon and operators, and machines                e.g. vehicles and machineries, using a biosensor or                wearable device in a computing device i.e. brain                computer interface (BCI) system (claimed). Uses                include but are not limited to a wirelessly                connected wearable or implantable devices such as a                BCI, functional magnetic resonance imaging (FMRI),                electroencephalography (EEG), or implantable brain                chips, motion remote gesture sensing controller,                breathing tube sip and puff controller and an                electrooculography (EOG) or eye gaze sensing                controller, in a military setting, a healthcare                setting, a virtual reality setting, a smart city                setting, a smart transportation setting, a smart                workplace setting, a smart education setting, a                smart entertainment setting, a smart finance                setting and a smart agriculture setting for gaming                and entertainment purpose, educational purposes                such as language learning or skill training                purposes, customer service purpose, research and                development purposes such as data analysis or                scientific discovery purpose and home automation                purpose.
                    ADVANTAGE - The AI system can be used to provide real-time                alerts and recommendations to the user based on the                data and to allow the user to control the virtual                environment using biosignals. The system supports                collecting and processing historical data from the                sensory device, system, subsystems and output                actions to improve performance and personalization                of the system, subsystems, and sensory devices. The                output of the generative AI or generalist agent                drives an output stage that is able to support and                facilitate the human agency of the user based on                the output, so that the user interacts with the                system with ease and rapidity, and the system                generates communications to or instructs the                actions of supportive and interactive entities                surrounding the user.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - The companion application is a                network-connected companion application. The                conversation engine includes at least one of a                conversation type classifier, an adjacency pair                classifier, a question classifier, a prompt                orchestration and a conversation language model.                The conversation partner is a machine agent. An                INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method for                enabling artificial intelligence (AI) assisted                conversation using biosensor.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a block diagram of a                language engine.120Conversation features124Conversation output200User experience engine300Conversation engine310Conversation language models500Memory engine502Local database800Language engine
